// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  A BARD'S TALE
//  A perchance.org recreation of the classic 1980s first-person, party-based
//  dungeon crawler — character creation, a 3D maze view, spells, turn-based
//  combat, a hub town with shops, and dungeons to explore.
//
//  ROADMAP:
//  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ## Phase 1: Core Engine & Grid State
//  Establish the fundamental game loop and spatial coordinate system.
//  1. [x] **Game State Object**: Define a global state object containing party data, current map, and player coordinates; verify by logging state to console.
//  2. [x] **Grid Movement Logic**: Implement a function to handle movement (forward, back, left, right) that updates X/Y coordinates and orientation; verify by printing coordinates to screen.
//  3. [x] **Map Generator (Basic)**: Create a system to generate a 2D array of integers (0=floor, 1=wall) with a guaranteed path from start to end; verify by rendering the array as a text grid.
//  4. [x] **Canvas Setup**: Initialize a full-screen canvas and a basic render loop; verify by drawing a static colored square.
//  5. [x] **Pseudo-3D Projection**: Implement a simple ray-casting or projection function to render the current grid cell's walls on the canvas; verify by moving through the grid and seeing walls shift.
//  6. [x] **Collision System**: Prevent the player from moving into cells marked as walls; verify by attempting to walk through a wall and remaining stationary.
//  
//  ## Phase 2: Party Architecture
//  Build the character system and statistical foundation.
//  7. [x] **Race/Class Definitions**: Create data objects for original races and classes with base stat modifiers; verify by printing a list of available options.
//  8. [x] **Character Generator**: Implement a "roll" system for the six core stats (STR, INT, DEX, CON, CHA, LUK); verify by creating a character and displaying their rolls.
//  9. [x] **Derived Stats Logic**: Calculate HP, Armor Class, and Mana based on stats and class; verify by ensuring a Warrior has more HP than a Magician.
//  10. [x] **Party Management**: Implement a party array (up to 4 members) with a "current party" state; verify by adding multiple characters to the party list.
//  11. [x] **Character Sheet UI**: Build an HTML overlay showing the party's stats and current HP/MP; verify by checking if values update during state changes.
//  
//  ## Phase 3: Exploration Mechanics
//  Add sensory and navigation depth to the dungeon.
//  12. [x] **Light Radius System**: Implement a "light level" variable that clips the canvas rendering based on distance from the player; verify by seeing walls fade to black in the distance.
//  13. [x] **Auto-Map UI**: Create a top-down 2D map that fills in as the player visits tiles; verify by moving to a new tile and seeing a dot appear on the map.
//  14. [x] **Interactive Objects**: Add "triggers" to the grid for doors, chests, and traps; verify by triggering a console message when stepping on a specific tile.
//  15. [x] **Door Logic**: Implement locked/unlocked states for doors requiring a key or a specific check; verify by blocking movement until a "key" flag is true.
//  
//  ## Phase 4: Combat Foundation
//  Implement the turn-based encounter system.
//  16. [x] **Encounter Trigger**: Create a random chance to trigger a combat state upon moving into a new cell; verify by entering combat randomly during movement.
//  17. [x] **Combat State Transition**: Create a UI switch that hides the 3D view and shows the Combat Panel (monster list vs party list); verify by entering and exiting combat.
//  18. [x] **Monster Database**: Define an original bestiary with scaling HP, Attack, and XP values; verify by spawning different monsters based on dungeon depth.
//  19. [x] **Turn Order Queue**: Implement a round-based system where each party member and monster acts in sequence; verify by logging the sequence of attacks.
//  20. [x] **Basic Attack Logic**: Implement a "hit/miss" calculation based on DEX and Monster AC; verify by seeing "Hit" or "Miss" messages in the combat log.
//  
//  ## Phase 5: Magic & Ability System
//  Develop the spellcasting mechanics.
//  21. [x] **Spell Database**: Create original spells categorized by class/tier with MP costs and effects; verify by listing spells available to a Conjurer.
//  22. [x] **Spell Casting UI**: Implement a menu-driven selection process for spells during combat; verify by selecting a spell and deducting MP.
//  23. [x] **Spell Effects**: Implement logic for damage, healing, and buffs; verify by seeing monster HP drop or party HP rise after a spell.
//  24. [x] **Mana Regeneration**: Create a system for recovering MP through resting or items; verify by checking MP increase after a "rest" action.
//  
//  ## Phase 6: The Hub Town
//  Build the non-combat social and economic layer.
//  25. [x] **Town Layout & Navigation**: Build the town map and a menu to choose its locations; verify by moving between town locations and back to the dungeon.
//  
//  ## Phase 7: Town Services & Economy
//  Implement the commercial and support systems of the hub town.
//  26. [x] **Currency System**: Implement a global party gold variable and a function to add/subtract gold; verify by checking gold balance in the UI.
//  27. [x] **Armory Shop**: Create a menu to buy/sell original weapons and armor with gold costs; verify by purchasing an item and seeing gold decrease.
//  28. [x] **Temple Services**: Implement a "Heal" and "Resurrect" service with a gold cost; verify by restoring party HP to max.
//  29. [x] **The Inn**: Create a resting mechanic that restores HP/MP and allows party reorganization; verify by triggering a "rest" state that refills bars.
//  30. [x] **Adventurer's Guild**: Implement a quest-board system that tracks completed objectives; verify by marking a "dungeon cleared" flag as true.
//  
//  ## Phase 8: Inventory & Equipment
//  Manage the physical assets and stat modifiers of the party.
//  31. [x] **Item Database**: Define a list of original consumables (potions, scrolls) and equipment (swords, shields) with stat modifiers; verify by listing item properties.
//  32. [x] **Inventory Grid**: Build a UI list showing all items currently held by the party; verify by adding an item to the list via the shop.
//  33. [x] **Equipment Slots**: Implement "Equip/Unequip" logic for Head, Body, and Weapon slots per character; verify by seeing a character's AC or Attack value increase.
//  34. [x] **Consumable Logic**: Create a function to use items from the inventory during exploration or combat; verify by using a potion to regain HP.
//  
//  ## Phase 9: Advanced Dungeon Design
//  Create complex environmental hazards and structural challenges.
//  35. [x] **Dungeon Tiering**: Create three distinct map sets (Low, Mid, Deep) with increasing monster difficulty; verify by transitioning to a "Deep" map.
//  36. [x] **Dark Rooms**: Implement "Pitch Black" tiles where the render distance is reduced to zero unless a torch is equipped; verify by walking into a black tile.
//  37. [x] **Trap Mechanics**: Implement floor-based traps (spikes, pits) that trigger damage or displacement; verify by taking damage upon entering a trap tile.
//  38. [x] **One-Way Doors**: Create "Valve" doors that allow entry from one side but not the other; verify by being unable to return to a previous tile.
//  39. [x] **Riddle Gates**: Implement text-based input prompts that require a keyword to unlock a door; verify by typing the correct answer to open a gate.
//  
//  ## Phase 10: Persistence & Audio
//  Integrate saving and sensory feedback.
//  40. [x] **Save/Load Integration**: Use the kv-plugin to serialize the game state object to local storage; verify by refreshing the page and retaining party stats.
//  41. [x] **Audio Manager**: Create a system to trigger sounds from the upload service for combat, movement, and town themes; verify by hearing a sound on a button click.
//  42. [x] **Dynamic BGM**: Implement a logic switch that changes background music based on location (Town vs. Dungeon); verify by hearing the track change on map transition.
//  
//  ## Phase 11: Visual Polish & UI
//  Transform the prototype into a finished product.
//  43. [x] **Enhanced 3D Visuals**: Add textures (via canvas patterns) or gradient shading to the walls and floors; verify by seeing non-solid colors in the 3D view.
//  44. [x] **Combat Animations**: Implement "shake" or "flash" effects on the canvas when damage is dealt; verify by seeing the screen shake during an attack.
//  45. [x] **UI Skinning**: Apply a consistent 80s-style CSS theme (black backgrounds, neon or gold borders, pixel fonts); verify by inspecting the visual style of the menus.
//  
//  ## Phase 12: Endgame & Balance
//  Finalize the victory condition and playability.
//  46. [x] **Final Boss Encounter**: Create a unique boss entity with a multi-stage attack pattern and high HP; verify by triggering the boss fight at the deepest tile.
//  47. [x] **Win Condition**: Implement a "Victory" screen and credits sequence upon defeating the boss; verify by reaching the end-game state.
//  48. [x] **Balance Pass**: Adjust XP curves and gold costs to ensure a 2-4 hour completion time; verify by playtesting a "speedrun" through the tiers.
//  
//  ## Sequence
//  1. **Core Engine & Grid** (Phases 1-3) -> **Combat & Magic** (Phases 4-5) ->
//     **Town & Economy** (Phases 6-8) -> **Deep Dungeons** (Phase 9) ->
//     **Persistence & Audio** (Phase 10) -> **Polish** (Phase 11) -> **Endgame & Balance** (Phase 12).
//  Gates: freeze movement/collision + stat rules before combat; freeze the bestiary and
//  spell list before dungeon design; freeze dungeon tier maps before the balance pass.
//  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

title
  A Bard's Tale

$meta
  title = A Bard's Tale
  description = A first-person, party-based dungeon crawler on Perchance: create a party of adventurers, explore a wireframe 3D maze city of dungeons, learn spells, fight monsters, and conquer the catacombs below. A fan-made homage to the classic Bard's Tale.
  image = https://user.uploads.dev/file/cce8d9467fc796c6427a2a0230ba30e3.png
  tags = rpg, dungeon, crawler, fantasy, game, retro
  header
    mode = minimal

kv = {import:kv-plugin}

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  GAME DATA — races, classes, stats. Tweak freely; the engine reads these
//  from the lists below at runtime. Everything here is original content.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

